  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>Five years on the most closely governed resource in the sector, asking the same forty-one questions of everyone who could be got to sit down. It produced the allocation instrument in its present form, a complete map of standing-water rights across the basin, and the first serious account of what becomes of those rights when a working closes. The one thing it never managed was to interview anybody at the evaporite workings, which failed and shut thirteen years later with the question still outstanding.</p>",
